## N13: versioned document nodes, Add to Knowledge Base, and webpage node actions

N13 adds the three node-level capabilities the canvas was missing: a document node's
version history with a real line diff (G18), "Add to Knowledge Base" from a run node,
and the actions only a webpage node has, open in the sandbox preview and download as a
ZIP (G19).

### Server
- `src/graph/versions.ts` - capture/list a node's versions and the exact LCS line diff
  between two of them.
- `src/graph/nodeVersions.ts` - capture the files a node names, so the archive stays
  complete after a canvas edit.
- `src/graph/artifacts.ts` - resolve a webpage node's directory against the task
  workspace and build the ZIP (one top-level folder named after the node).
- `src/knowledge/fromNode.ts` - split a node's text into Knowledge Garden seeds with
  honest node provenance (run id, node type, node version, split mode).
- `src/server/routes/graphNodes.ts` - `/api/graph/:runId/nodes/:nodeId/{versions,diff,
  knowledge,knowledge/preview,artifact,artifact.zip,preview}`. Every path is resolved
  against the task workspace, so a node id from another run cannot reach a different
  task's files.
- `src/graph/runGraph.ts` - node version bumps and the text/file capture hooks the
  agent calls as it works.

### Web
- `canvas/client.ts` - `getNodeVersions`, `getNodeDiff`, `captureNodeVersion`,
  `previewNodeKnowledge`, `addToKnowledgeBase`, `getNodeArtifact`, `startNodePreview`,
  `downloadNodeZip`, `listKnowledgeBases`, plus `canUseNodeActions` / `canOpenWebpage`.
- `canvas/nodeActions.ts` - the reply types and hand coercion for every one of them, so
  a partial or older reply still renders something honest.
- `canvas/DiffView.tsx` - the aligned diff, coloured by op, `dir="auto"` per line.
- `canvas/VersionPanel.tsx` - the version list, the two-version selection (defaulting to
  "what did I change last?"), capture, and the diff.
- `canvas/KnowledgePanel.tsx` - the seed preview *before* anything is written, then the
  add, then the result naming the base the seeds landed in.
- `canvas/WebpageActions.tsx` - open in the sandbox preview and download the ZIP.
- `CanvasPanel.tsx` - the three panels wired into the node detail sheet, and the
  `kb_seed` node label.
- i18n - 28 keys added to `en.json`/`ar.json` and the `en.ts`/`ar.ts` mirrors.

### Gates (measured)
- `npx tsc --noEmit`                            -> exit 0
- `node --import tsx --test "src/**/*.test.ts"` -> 2846 tests / 2846 pass / 0 fail
- `(cd packages/web && vitest run)`             -> 86 files / 592 tests, all passed
- `npm run build:server`                        -> exit 0 (server bundle + pdf worker)
- `(cd packages/web && npx next build)`         -> exit 0 (25/25 static pages)
- `npm run verify`                              -> exit 0 (typecheck, encoding, eval,
  orchestrator, recovery, modes)

### Notes
- `packages/web/src/i18n/lint.mjs` is broken at HEAD (`readdirSync` is handed a `URL`),
  so it cannot be run as a gate. This is pre-existing and outside N13's scope. The N13
  components were checked by running `audit.mjs` directly: the only findings are
  `data-testid` / `dir` / `target` values, which every existing component trips too. No
  user-facing string is hard-coded.
- `en.ts` / `ar.ts` are generated mirrors that lag `en.json` (704 keys behind at HEAD).
  All 28 N13 keys are present in all four files, and `en.json` / `ar.json` hold the same
  947-key set.
- No test was weakened, deleted or skipped. No secrets committed.
